       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Nothing in the details you gave (normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify going above that. A dose this high raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and it usually doesn't work better than 200 mg.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n\n1. **Typo or unit error.** You may have meant 40 mg or 100 mg. The usual start is 25\u201350 mg daily, titrated by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least a week, up to 200 mg.\n2. **Intentional dose.** If a psychiatry consultant or a specific protocol recommended it, tell me the dose and the rationale. I can enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n3. **Different intent.** If you meant a different drug or schedule, tell me and I'll adjust.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away. For example, I can enter 200 mg PO once daily, or a lower titration dose."
      }
